WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.340
[Sansa] Stop it!

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.870
You're spoiling it, you're spoiling everything!

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.490
I find it really concerning sometimes, how
many anime series have this one character

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.620
that is objectively an absolute piece of garbage
as a human being and yet SOMEHOW, ends up

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.000
as one of the my favorite characters.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.570
That's exactly how I felt the moment when
Toji entered Dagon's domain through the opening

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.970
everyone had just hoped to escape from.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:23.970
Can anyone relate?

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:29.260
Well, Let me also tell you the moment my opinion
of Toji Fushiguro was completely flipped on

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.240
his head.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.890
The destroyed city of Shibuya.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.230
The air thick with death, fear and chaos.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.300
Sukuna's presence is piercing the air, and
yet here, in this small side alley somewhere

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.530
on the battlefield, cramped between two buildings,
a father and son stand in front of each other

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.579
without even knowing who the other is.

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:54.530
Megumi not remembering his father, that abandoned
him as a child, now fully focused on getting

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.440
away from the monster that just easily took
out one of the special grades without so much

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.550
as an inch of cursed energy.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.920
Toji on the the other hand, a mindless beast
on a killing spree, who despite all the powerful

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.819
people on the battlefield, has chosen Megumi
as the strongest opponent.

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:16.779
Having just barely missed Megumis heart, he
prepares for another deadly jab.

00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:19.490
But suddenly a memory pierces his mind.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:24.389
A memory of how he sold his only Son to the
family he hated so much.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:28.929
And in the next moment, despite the cursed
technique controlling him, he takes control

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:35.149
again and ends his own life a second time
with a smile on his face.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:37.459
And I had tears in my eyes.

00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:44.289
Tears because of the emotions, but also tears
of joy for how criminally well this man is

00:01:44.289 --> 00:01:45.289
written.

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:55.849
I had finally understood who Toji Fushiguro
truly is as 

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.849
a character.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:02.789
For me, Toji is and always was strong contender
in the categories shittiest shonen fathers

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:07.389
and side characters that are already dead,
but somehow feel more exciting than some of

00:02:07.389 --> 00:02:08.920
those that are still alive.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.219
The core philosophy that Akutami gives Toji
is basically not giving a fuck.

00:02:14.219 --> 00:02:18.610
We are being told that Toji doesn't care about
anything or anyone.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.459
He doesn't care about his family, going his
own way and doing his own thing.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:27.620
He goes through weapons at an alarming rate,
no matter if it's a cheap gun or a priceless

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:35.209
cursed weapon, when you think about it, you
never see Toji using the same tool twice,

00:02:35.209 --> 00:02:38.060
just switching to a new one whenever he needs
to.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:43.010
He doesn't care about his son and even about
his own life, readily prepared to throw it

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.030
away, just to make a point.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.800
When I first read the hidden inventory arc,
not in my wildest dreams did I expect that

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.900
this sketchy looking guy, that is supposed
to be Megumi's dead, I mean dad, would be

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.819
one of the most influential, powerful and
deep characters of the story.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:04.409
It didn't take long however for Toji to get
my full attention, when he is revealed as

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:09.099
the mastermind behind the attack on Riko,
a girl meant to fuse with the immortal sorcerer

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:14.640
Tengen so he could remain human.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.550
Fully aware that Riko is with Gojo and Geto,
the two most powerful sorcerers in the country

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.629
right now, who are in charge of protecting
the girl until the ritual, he cleverly keeps

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:26.659
throwing diversions at them from behind the
scenes.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:31.290
He patiently waits until Gojo is so tired
out from constantly being on guard with his

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.999
six eyes so he can launch a surprise attack
on both.

00:03:34.999 --> 00:03:39.959
And even though Gojo was of course already
an absolute favorite of mine at this point,

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:45.219
Toji's fighting style and underdog status
made it hard not to be impressed by him, as

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:50.200
he manages to take out all three of his targets,
apparently even killing Gojo.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:56.069
And despite how much of a dick he was, abandoning
his son to gamble, drink and fight, the only

00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:01.239
thing I thought was that this guy is purely
badass.

00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:07.340
At first glance, the fight between Gojo and
Toji may seem like that of two powerful maniacs,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:13.739
but it's actually based on Chinese mythology:
The godly Buddha and the chaotic monkey king.

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:19.630
Gojo, who literally quotes the buddy after
surviving his stabbing, has reached some sort

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.880
of enlightenment, now fully aware of the true
nature of cursed energy and basically from

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.910
this moment onwards unstoppable.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:33.630
He sees everything and is one with the world,
able to manipulate space itself.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:39.090
His domain expansion literally forces the
universes true nature onto you, once you are

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.620
caught in it.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:53.009
And, as he puts it himself, coming back from
certain death, he is practically reborn in

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:55.800
the infinite cycle of reincarnation.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.569
Toji meanwhile represents Sun Wukong, who
rebelled against the gods.

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:07.669
Toji literally likes to call himself a monkey
for not having cursed energy, basically making

00:05:07.669 --> 00:05:10.750
fun of Geto, before he even goes mad.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.580
Just like the monkey king, he is exiled from
the heavenly order of the 4 clans.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:21.479
Later on, we see him fully mastering playful
cloud, just as Sun Wukong, was known for using

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:24.720
a staff and flying on top of a cloud.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.379
Ultimately, just like in 'the journey to the
west' the Buddha HIMSELF has to put an end

00:05:29.379 --> 00:05:36.520
to his rebellion, just like Gojo is the only
who could have stopped Toji.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:45.000
And when Gojo has launched his new attack,
hollow purple, and i turned the page, my entire

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.000
perspective on Toji completley changed.

